--- /dev/null
+++ b/PORT_NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# sR Port Notes
+
+- **Fidelity Note**: Using the unique sequence ID instead of a physical ROB tag implies the digest table payload holds larger values, requiring care with bit limits.
+- **Fidelity Note**: All floating-point instructions are digested using the FP64 extraction rule, which misinterprets the sign and exponent bits for FP32/16 results.
+- **Fidelity Note**: The predictor never observes squashes, so pending register writes are never cleared due to squash, diverging from real hardware behavior.
